---
import LegalLayout from "../layouts/LegalLayout.astro";
import { EMPRESA, ENVIO_GRATIS } from "../data/empresa";
const H = (t: string) => `<span class="hueco">${t}</span>`;
---

<LegalLayout title="Shipping" kicker="LEGAL · SHIPPING">

  <h2>The short version</h2>
  <p>
    We prepare your order within 24 business hours and it arrives in 48 to 72 business hours. Over
    ${ENVIO_GRATIS}, shipping is on us. You get a tracking link by email the moment it leaves.
  </p>

  <h2>Where we ship</h2>
  <p>
    We currently ship to
    <span set:html={EMPRESA.envios.startsWith("[") ? H(EMPRESA.envios) : EMPRESA.envios} />.
    If your country is not on that list yet, join the mailing list — we announce new destinations
    there first.
  </p>

  <h2>Times and costs</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Preparation:</strong> within 24 business hours of your order.</li>
    <li><strong>Delivery:</strong> 48 to 72 business hours after that, for standard destinations.</li>
    <li><strong>Free shipping</strong> on orders over ${ENVIO_GRATIS}. Below that, a flat $6.95 within the contiguous US — you see it at checkout before you pay.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Business hours means working days. An order placed on Friday evening is prepared on Monday.
    Public holidays and peak periods can add a day, and we would rather say so here than surprise you.
  </p>

  <h2>Membership boxes</h2>
  <p>
    The Burrow works on a single monthly cut-off, not on your individual join date. Members are
    charged at the start of the month and the boxes go out together in the first week. That is
    deliberate: it means everyone receives that month's card at roughly the same time.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you join mid-month, your first box goes out with the next cut-off, and we tell you the date
    when you subscribe.
  </p>

  <h2>Tracking</h2>
  <p>
    As soon as the parcel is collected you receive an email with the carrier and the tracking number.
    The same information is in your account, under MY BURROW. Tracking can take a few hours to start
    updating after you receive it; that is the carrier's system, not a lost parcel.
  </p>

  <h2>If the address is wrong</h2>
  <p>
    We ship to the address you enter, exactly as you enter it. If you spot a mistake, write to
    <a href={`mailto:${EMPRESA.email}`}>{EMPRESA.email}</a> immediately — if the parcel has not left,
    we fix it for free. Once it has been collected we cannot change it, and a reshipment to a
    corrected address is charged again.
  </p>

  <h2>Parcels that come back to us</h2>
  <p>
    If a parcel is returned because nobody collected it or the address was incomplete, we contact you.
    You can have it sent again, paying the new shipping, or take a refund of the products minus the
    original shipping cost.
  </p>

  <h2>Lost or damaged in transit</h2>
  <p>
    If tracking stops moving for more than 7 business days, or the box arrives damaged, tell us. We
    open the claim with the carrier — that is our job, not yours — and we send a replacement or refund
    you. You do not wait for the carrier to decide before we resolve it.
  </p>

  <h2>Customs and duties</h2>
  <p>
    For international destinations, any import duties or taxes charged by your country are set by your
    customs authority and paid by you on delivery. We cannot calculate them in advance or mark a
    parcel as a gift to avoid them.
  </p>

  <h2>Heat, cold and drinks</h2>
  <p>
    Rabbit Fuel travels well, but cans do not enjoy being left in a freezing porch for two days. If
    you are ordering to a place with extreme weather, consider having it delivered somewhere it can be
    collected the same day.
  </p>

</LegalLayout>
